From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 20:10:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 61/74] fix(gastown): warn when the step re-point cannot
 re-read its new bead (gcp-5gir)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review touch-up on the STEP_REPOINTED path added by 421663c.

After the re-point swaps WORK_ID to the molecule's next ready step, the
block re-reads that bead into SHOW_JSON. If that read fails, SHOW_JSON is
empty and the block's closing `jq` silently prints nothing — the polecat
gets a CLAIMED_BEAD_ID with no metadata beneath it and no indication that
anything went wrong. Say so explicitly instead, and name the command that
recovers it. The re-point itself is unaffected: the claim already landed,
so this is a reporting gap, not a control-flow one.
---
 gastown/agents/polecat/prompt.template.md | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gastown/agents/polecat/prompt.template.md b/gastown/agents/polecat/prompt.template.md
index 4640481..ee46623 100644
--- a/gastown/agents/polecat/prompt.template.md
+++ b/gastown/agents/polecat/prompt.template.md
@@ -267,6 +267,8 @@ if [ -z "$STEP_REF" ]; then
     echo "STEP_REPOINTED hook returned work bead $WORK_ID; this session is mid-molecule, continuing with step $NEXT_STEP_ID"
     WORK_ID="$NEXT_STEP_ID"
     SHOW_JSON="$(gc bd show "$WORK_ID" --json 2>/dev/null)"
+    [ -n "$SHOW_JSON" ] ||
+      echo "WARN could not re-read $WORK_ID; run 'gc bd show $WORK_ID' before you start the step"
   fi
   # No ready step means the molecule has nothing runnable right now: keep the
   # work bead, read your formula steps, and let the done sequence decide.
